MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_001: Oh, sweet, sweet madazins. I'm gonna take my time\neating all this good stuff.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_002: *sigh*
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_003: Oh, Ursula...
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_004: What should I do here? She's always so cold.\nIt makes me nervous.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_005: She's this big-time business person. It'd be a bad\nidea to just ignore her, right? OK, here goes...
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_006: Uhm... H-hello.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_007: Oh, hello, Peter. Doing well, I hope?
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_008: You're in a fun mood. Did something good happen?
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_009: I've just acquired a painting by an artist I have a\nparticular fondness for. It was not easy to come by.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_010: I was able to use my connections through Vandahl\nTrading to place a bid before it hit the open market.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_011: Must be a special painting if you went to all\nthat trouble.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_012: It's a spectacular piece. The soul of the artist is\nalive in every brushstroke.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_013: The dealer is arranging a special delivery for me\nnow. I can hardly wait for it to arrive.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_014: You're really into paintings, huh? Are you an artist?
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_015: I enjoy sketching during my days off.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_016: Yeah? You get some days off?
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_017: Hehe. I do. Even I have to take a break every\nnow and again.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_018: {SetColor=Gray}She laughed! I guess she has a friendly side.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_019: Do you think...I might be able to watch you\ndraw sometime?
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_020: There isn't much to see... But you're welcome to\nwatch, if you'd like.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_C_021: Thanks! And I think it'll be great!
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_001: *sigh*
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_002: Wow! You turned the scenery in front of you into a\npicture so fast!
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_003: Ursula, you were being modest before. You're really\ngood at this.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_004: Oh, I don't think it's anything special—but that's\nvery kind of you to say, Peter.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_005: Hehe... I don't know about "kind." I'm more...timid,\nand that's never done me any good.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_006: This old guy in my village always yelled at me\nbecause I was bad at hunting by nature.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_007: I'd fall behind everyone else, and I'd make mistakes\nall the time.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_008: Hm. Perhaps we're not so different.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_009: I was insecure as a child as well.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_010: Huh? That's hard to imagine.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_011: You've got yourself together. You can talk really\nwell... You're impressive.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_012: I wasn't always. I used to struggle to put my thoughts\ninto words in a way others could understand.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_013: That's why I learned to draw. My late father taught\nme, so I could speak even when words failed me.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_014: {SetColor=Gray}Huh. Her father taught her to draw. Kinda like mine\ntaught me how to use a bow.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_015: My father taught me the basics, and my mother\npraised my efforts.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_016: And now, I draw to remember them, to feel close\nto my parents again.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_017: I get it. When my dad taught me archery, it gave me\na confidence boost.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_018: Then that's another way in which you and I are not\nso different...
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_019: If we'd met as children, I have a feeling we would\nhave been friends.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_020: Yeah, probably.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_021: But we can be friends now, Ursula. If you want.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_022: I suppose we can. And it would be my\npleasure, Peter.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_023: To celebrate our friendship, I'll just make a few\nsmall changes to this sketch...
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_024: Whoa! Is this me and you, chatting away?
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_025: It is! And when I'm finished, I want you to have it.
MID_SE_Pet_Urs_B_026: Are you serious? I'd love that! I promise I'll take good\ncare of it!